-- title:
--   Newform λ-adic representation is special at q ‖ M
-- statement:
--   Fix $M \neq 0$ and a cusp form $g$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform (its $q$-expansion coefficients satisfy $a_1 = 1$, multiplicativity at coprime indices, and the usual two-term recursions at primes dividing and not dividing $M$) and for no proper divisor of $M$ does there exist a normalised eigenform of that level agreeing with $g$ at all primes $\ell \nmid M$. Fix a prime $\lambda$, a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$, and a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}'$ with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra M 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) (the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(M)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid M$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid M$, $q \notin S$) to $\mathbb{C}$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell) = a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal{O}'$. Let $q \neq \lambda$ be a prime with $q \mid M$ and $q^2 \nmid M$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with $q$ a non-unit of $P$. Then there is a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain $\mathcal{O}''$ with finite residue field, finite over $\mathcal{O}'$ by an injective local algebra map, and a [`GaloisRepAdic`](def/GaloisRep_Adic.html#L16) $\rho$ over $\mathcal{O}''$, that is a free $\mathcal{O}''$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\rho$ from $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}''}(V)$ which is adically continuous (for each $n$ some finite subextension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ has the property that elements fixing $L$ pointwise act trivially on $V/\mathfrak{m}^n V$), such that: for every prime $\ell \nmid M$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $\ell \neq \lambda$, every valuation subring $A$ with $\ell$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $A$ inducing $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$ on the residue field of $A$, the characteristic polynomial of $\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \iota(\chi_g(T_\ell)) X + \ell$; and there are a submodule $L \subseteq V$ and $a \in \{1, -1\}$ with $a_q(g) = a$ in $\mathbb{C}$, with $L = \mathcal{O}'' \cdot b_0$ for some $\mathcal{O}''$-basis $(b_0, b_1)$ of $V$, such that $L$ is stable under the decomposition group of $P$, every element $\tau$ of the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia group of $P$ fixes $L$ pointwise and satisfies $\rho(\tau)v - v \in L$ for all $v \in V$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition group of $P$ inducing $x \mapsto x^{q}$ on the residue field acts on $L$ by multiplication by $aq$ and satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - a v \in L$ for all $v \in V$.
--
--   This is the statement that the $\lambda$-adic representation attached to a weight-two newform is special (Steinberg-type, up to an unramified twist) at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level, the unramified quotient character sending Frobenius at $q$ to $a_q(g) = \pm 1$, in the existence form that also produces the coefficient ring $\mathcal{O}''$ and records the characteristic polynomials of Frobenius away from $M$, $S$ and $\lambda$. It supplies the local behaviour at $q$ used in the construction of $\lambda$-adic representations with prescribed local data at a prime exactly dividing the level, and is cited by [`CuspForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_of_point_stableLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_of_isUnit_U`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_galoisRepAdic_of_point_stableLine_frobenius_sub_smul_mem_of_isUnit_U) and [`GaloisRepAdic.exists_stableLine_frobenius_eq_qCoeff_smul_of_isNewform_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd`](thm.html#GaloisRepAdic.exists_stableLine_frobenius_eq_qCoeff_smul_of_isNewform_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd).
